<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Siege of Alexandria</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Adora Diana Minor&lt;/b&gt; is a young patrician woman of the influential Roman &lt;i&gt;gens Julia&lt;/i&gt;. The daughter of the governor of Syria and niece to Caesar is sent to Egypt to strengthen the Julian bonds to the important Roman ally through an unwanted marriage. Can Adora find a way out of this?&lt;br /&gt;&lt;b&gt;Catra Meritamun&lt;/b&gt; is an Egyptian noblewoman of Nubian heritage. She rules a settlement and fortress at the Nile on behalf of Pharaoh Cleopatra. She is called to the Egyptian royal court to fulfill her duties to the realm. Soon, Catra will have to make a terrible decision.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;This is a heavily drama loaded #Catradora in Ancient Egypt AU. It's about their paths through a turning point of history, and they'll witness, and take part in some of the most important events of this time. How did Cleopatra and Caesar met? Was Alexandria the only thing to be besieged? How can Adora and Catra prevail against the forces that helped empires to glory and turned them into ashes?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;And did Catra set the world on fire?&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;(It is relatively fandom-blind, so you can read this even if you don't know anything about the fandom.)&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>21st_tikonda</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
